          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP Is Awesome: Standardized Content Integration"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "52070ae5-cb46-4403-a3ec-5a8bc9053660",
              "mediaKey": "52070ae5-cb46-4403-a3ec-5a8bc9053660",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "content",
          "value": {
            "markup": "<p>MCP (Model Context Protocol) revolutionizes how we integrate content management with AI systems. Instead of building custom API layers and authentication schemes for every tool, MCP provides a standardized interface that works seamlessly across platforms.</p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Unified Interface:</strong> Work with documents, media, and content through consistent protocols</li><li><strong>Reduced Complexity:</strong> No more custom integrations—MCP handles the heavy lifting</li><li><strong>Type Safety:</strong> Full schema awareness means fewer runtime errors and better tooling</li><li><strong>Seamless Automation:</strong> Agents can inspect, modify, and publish content without special configuration</li></ul><p>Whether you're building content workflows, automating editorial processes, or integrating with AI systems, MCP provides the foundation for modern content management infrastructure.</p>",
            "blocks": {
